'''Trinkets''' are a type of collectible with their designated slot that can provide passive bonuses. Only one trinket can be carried at a time and must be dropped if you wish to carry another. Some of these limitations can be bypassed with certain [[item]]s; {{i|Mom's Purse}} and {{i|Belly Button}} allow two trinkets to be held at once, {{dlc|a+|}} and trinkets can be absorbed by {{i|Smelter}}, {{i|Marbles}}, or [[Gulp!]]. Absorbed trinkets do not take up a trinket slot and act as permanent passive effects.

Compared to items with a similar effect, trinket effects are typically more subtle, less powerful, or less reliable. For example, the {{t|Callus}} only prevents damage from spikes and creep, while many items that do the same also grant Isaac [[flight]].

The original Binding of Isaac DLC 'The Wrath of the Lamb' introduced Trinkets as a mechanic and had 33 trinkets. Rebirth has a total of 60 trinkets. [[Afterbirth]] added 29 new trinkets, for a total of 89 trinkets. [[Afterbirth †]] added 38 new trinkets, for a total of 127 trinkets. [[The Binding of Isaac: Repentance|Repentance]] added 61 new trinkets, for a total of 188 trinkets.

{{dlc|r}} All trinkets have a very rare 2% chance to spawn as [[Golden Trinket]]s.

* Unlocked by: {{achievement unlock|Golden Trinket}}

== Notes ==
* It is possible to drop a trinket by holding down the key or button bound to the "Drop" function for three seconds. (Doing this is not possible with the {{t|Tick}}.)
* While held, {{i|Mom's Box}} doubles the effect of most trinkets.
** {{dlc|r}} A Golden Trinket with Mom's Box will have a tripled effect.
* Trinkets appear in a set order based on the run's seed, and each trinket can usually only be encountered once.
** Trinkets which are set drops, such as {{t|Mysterious Paper}} from {{i|Divorce Papers}} and {{t|The Left Hand}} from {{e|Ultra Pride}}, can appear even if encountered previously.
** Other set drops, such as {{t|Swallowed Penny}} from a [[urn]] or {{t|Umbilical Cord}} from a [[polyp]], will not appear if already seen.
** If enough trinkets are spawned, e.g. through Mom's Box, the cycle loops and begins spawning trinkets that were already encountered.
* {{dlc|nr}} If two of the same trinkets are gathered, Isaac can have both by using [[Gulp!]] on one and then picking up the other. This rarely has any useful purpose.
* {{dlc+|r}} Multiples of the same trinkets sometimes stack as expected, and two copies of the same trinket can be held simultaneously with {{i|Belly Button}} or {{i|Mom's Purse}}. However, a large number of trinkets don't stack, especially the ones that are more complicated than a simple stat up.{{dlc-}}
* Trinkets cannot be duplicated with items such as {{i|Diplopia}} or {{P|Jera}}.
* {{dlc+|a+nr}} Activating the {{i|D1}} on a trinket will duplicate the trinket.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|r}} Activating the {{i|D1}} on a trinket will spawn a new, different trinket.{{dlc-}}

